  Root-cause fix recorded for honesty: the first view drafts crashed the WinUI XAML markup compiler
  (WMC9999 "Object reference not set", cascading WMC0001/WMC0110 across unrelated pre-existing XAML). Bisected to a
  `using Windows.System;` (added for VirtualKey) that made `DispatcherQueue` ambiguous with
  Microsoft.UI.Dispatching.DispatcherQueue (CS0104); the markup compiler null-refs on the unresolved type instead of
  reporting cleanly. Fixed by dropping the using and fully-qualifying Windows.System.VirtualKey. Verified by a
  pristine-tree build (0/0) and incremental re-introduction.

